Figure 5b shows the observed distribution of pitch angle $\upalpha,$ , which is the angle between a tangent to the superhelical curve and the coiled-coil axis. Once again, this is not a completely free parameter and is related to $R_{0}$ and ${\bf{\omega}}_{\omega_{0}}$ via Eq. 1. The peak of the distribution is at around $12~^{\circ}$ . For both pitch angle and superhelical frequency, the peak values are very close to the values that best fit the coiled-coil region of the yeast transcription factor $\mathrm{GCN4}^{43}$ —the first high-resolution structure of a parallel dimeric coiled coil as well as one that has long served as the prototypical coiled-coil example. It is interesting that in Crick parametric terms, this structure is indeed prototypical.
